{
  "result": "Okay, speaking for myself then.\n\nI wouldn't choose a superpower or an ending to a specific problem. I'd change something smaller, underneath a lot of them:\n\nI'd make people stay curious about each other a little longer than they stay defensive.\n\nThat split-second moment when someone says something we hate, or hurts us, or seems completely alien \u2014 I'd stretch it. Long enough to wonder, honestly: *What is it like to be you? What are you afraid of? What made this make sense to you?*\n\nNot agree. Not excuse. Just *see* first.\n\nSo much cruelty doesn't come from people being evil in that moment. It comes from them going numb, or certain, or tribal, really fast. Fear becomes certainty. Certainty becomes contempt. Contempt makes anything permissible.\n\nIf curiosity won that first race, even by a few seconds, I think families, friendships, politics, the internet... they'd all start to sound different. Harder to dehumanize someone you've actually imagined from the inside.\n\nThat's the world I'd pick.",
